  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1055" flags="0x0">
    <title>Fuel Blend - MAP-&gt;Throttle Threshold (vs RPM)</title>
    <description>Throttle angle at which base fuel starts handing over from the IAP (vacuum) maps to the TPS maps, vs engine speed. FUN_491BC: w = clamp((TP + width - threshold) x 256 / width) with width = 16 &lt;&lt; (Fuel Blend :: MAP-&gt;Throttle Ramp Width), stock 1024 counts = 2.8 deg; final base fuel = IAP_map x (256-w) + TPS_map x w (weight fef011CA). Stock thresholds 15-38 deg. Raise a cell to keep the IAP maps in charge to a larger throttle opening at that rpm, lower it to hand over to the TPS maps earlier. Above the WOT gate (Fuel Blend - WOT Throttle-Path Gate, 91.4 deg) the TPS maps always have 100% authority. Sensor-fault limp-home (FUN_36976/FUN_3A96C) forces w = 256. Axis input is fef0259C (engine speed, X/2.56).

REFERENCE: data @0x154E20 (10 x 16-bit), X axis @0x154E0C, descriptor @0x154E34, code FUN_491bc.</description>
