  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x10BD" flags="0x0">
    <title>IAP - In Gear | Cyl 3</title>
    <description>Main IAP (manifold-vacuum based) base fuel map for cylinder 3 while in gear with the clutch released. Output is a raw fuel quantity (injection time units) indexed by manifold vacuum and RPM.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: Code: FUN_45320 looks up...

AXES: X axis: 30 points, 78.1 down to 0.0 kPa VACUUM (0 = atmospheric / WOT, 78 = high vacuum / closed throttle); Y axis: 50 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ30): 512 to 4745 fuel qty (raw).

TUNING NOTES: This is the cylinder 3 IAP fuel map you would normally tune. Changes here affect cylinder 3 only, so keep the four cylinder maps consistent unless you are correcting a cylinder-to-cylinder imbalance. HOW IT IS COMBINED: final base fuel = IAP_map x (256 - w) + TPS_map x w, where w (fef011CA) comes from FUN_491BC: w = 0 (100% this IAP map) below the "Fuel Blend - MAP-&gt;Throttle Threshold (vs RPM)" throttle angle, ramps to 256 over the next ~2.8 deg (Fuel Blend :: MAP-&gt;Throttle Ramp Width), and is forced to 256 (100% TPS map) at/above the WOT gate (0x1824C6, 91.4 deg). So at light/part throttle this map fuels the engine; at large throttle openings and WOT the TPS map does.

REFERENCE: data @0x162D08, X axis @0x155E24, Y axis @0x162CA4, descriptor @0x155E60, code FUN_45320. [Shortened for TunerPro - full text in stock/xdf-master.]</description>
