  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x10C9" flags="0x0">
    <title>IAP - Neutral/Clutch-In | Cyl 1</title>
    <description>IAP base fuel map for cylinder 1 used while in NEUTRAL or with the CLUTCH PULLED (free-revving, blips, warm-up idle).

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_4543E uses this map when flag 0xFEF0271D bit0 (gear = neutral OR clutch switch on) has been set for at least 3 cycles (counter &gt;= 0x182703 = 3) and option 0x1826E8 != 3; otherwise it passes the in-gear result through.

AXES: X axis: 30 points, 78.1 down to 0.0 kPa VACUUM (0 = atmospheric / WOT, 78 = high vacuum / closed throttle); Y axis: 50 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ30): 535 to 4872 fuel qty (raw).

TUNING NOTES: Tune for idle quality and free-rev response. Has no effect when riding in gear with the clutch out.

CONFIDENCE: Confirmed from code.

REFERENCE: data @0x16BEB8, X axis @0x156244, Y axis @0x16BE54, descriptor @0x156280, code FUN_4543e.</description>
