  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x10DF" flags="0x0">
    <title>TPS - In Gear | Cyl 4</title>
    <description>Main alpha-N (throttle based) base fuel map for cylinder 4 while in gear with the clutch released. Output is a raw fuel quantity (injection time units) indexed by throttle angle and RPM.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: Code: FUN_4536c looks up all six maps of the cylinder 4 set (pointer table 0x17EBE4, index cyl*6+n); FUN_453B8 then uses map 1 as the result, blended with map 2 by a weight that is hard-coded to 0, so this map is the one that actually fuels cylinder 4. In neutral / clutch-in the "TPS - Neutral/Clutch-In | Cyl 4" map is used instead. Was "TPS - User Mode | Gear 1" in the DanCycles naming.

AXES: X axis: 26 points, 0.46 to 118 deg (abs. TP angle); Y axis: 50 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ30): 454 to 5257 raw (inj. time?).

TUNING NOTES: This is the cylinder 4 TPS fuel map you would normally tune. Changes here affect cylinder 4 only, so keep the four cylinder maps consistent unless you are correcting a cylinder-to-cylinder imbalance. How the TPS and IAP results are combined downstream has not been traced yet - change one family at a time and log.

REFERENCE: data @0x17AD00, X axis @0x156944, Y axis @0x17AC9C, descriptor @0x156978, code FUN_4536c. [Shortened for TunerPro - full text in stock/xdf-master.]</description>
