  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1132" flags="0x0">
    <title>IGN :: Trim B | Neutral/Clutch-In (user retard map, inactive stock)</title>
    <description>Ignition timing trim map (throttle angle x RPM, 8-bit). 64 raw = 0 deg (no change).

HOW THE ECU USES IT: Used while in neutral or with the clutch pulled. Looked up by FUN_52526 / FUN_525EE / FUN_525A0 / FUN_5262A (throttle angle 0xFEF02602 x RPM 0xFEF0155C); all trim outputs and the base advance are initialised to 64 (0x40) in FUN_51B02,...

AXES: X axis: 23 points, 0.00 to 117 deg (abs. TP angle); Y axis: 39 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ30): 0.00 to 0.00 deg RETARD (+ = retard, 64 raw = 0) - every cell the same, so the function is probably disabled or unused in this calibration.

TUNING NOTES: Trim values ABOVE 64 RETARD the spark (0.3516 deg per count). The trim output is a retard FLOOR (FUN_5171C takes the MAX of all retard sources, then FUN_517B4 subtracts it from the main advance) - it does not stack with traction/other retards. Stock every cell = 64 and the enable weight "IGN :: Trim B Enable Weight vs ECT" (0x1828C0) = 0, so this map does nothing until you raise that weight (128 = 100%). Useful as a spare throttle x RPM retard map. Not applied on the idle/neutral timing path (fef01544).

REFERENCE: data @0x188214, X axis @0x1848FC, Y axis @0x186F04, descriptor @0x1830EC, code FUN_525ee. [Shortened for TunerPro - full text in stock/xdf-master.]</description>
