  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x113B" flags="0x0">
    <title>IGN :: Advance Timing - Cyl 1</title>
    <description>Base ignition advance for cylinder 1, throttle angle x RPM.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_52688 looks up the cylinder's map (pointer table 0x182AF8[cyl]); if option byte 0x18B72E = 2 the Cyl 1 map is used for all cylinders (stock 0x80 = per-cylinder). Result -&gt; RAM 0xFEF0154C[cyl].

AXES: X axis: 23 points, 0.00 to 117 deg (abs. TP angle); Y axis: 39 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ30): 14.38 to 74.16 deg BTDC (OBD scale).

TUNING NOTES: Displayed as degrees BTDC using the scale the ECU uses to report timing on OBD (PID 0x0E): deg = (X-64)*0.3516 + 7. The 255 cells at very light load / high RPM are a ceiling and are not normally reached under load. Add advance cautiously; this is a 1340 cc high-compression engine.

CONFIDENCE: Scale derived from FUN_556CA (OBD timing byte = 0x80 + 14 + (X-64)*90/128). Replaces the old DanCycles 0.4X-12.5 guess.

REFERENCE: data @0x18A1B8, X axis @0x184A1C, Y axis @0x1870E4, descriptor @0x1831E8, code FUN_52688.</description>
