  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1278" flags="0x0">
    <title>Launch Control - Throttle Limit | Neutral, Gear 1</title>
    <description>Launch-control throttle LIMIT map (cap) for neutral, gear 1.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_7C8C2 looks it up via gear-indexed pointer table 0x18FD44; FUN_7C944 applies it as min(limit, normal target) when ETV control state 0xFEF02AF2 = 4. FUN_7C8F4 sets state 4 only when launch control is armed/active (RAM 0xFEF00702 bit2, copied from the LC-active bit0 by FUN_28D1E) and no TC/anti-lift limit has priority.

AXES: X axis: 23 points, 0.00 to 107 deg (abs. accel angle); Y axis: 39 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock 5JCZSJ30): 0.00 to 98.30 throttle angle (deg).

TUNING NOTES: This is the throttle part of launch control: while LC is active the throttle plate can never open past this map, whatever the grip angle. The RPM part is a fuel-cut limiter (see Launch Control constants). Lower cells = softer launch / less wheelie; raise toward the normal ETV map to let LC rely only on the RPM limiter.

CONFIDENCE: Confirmed from code; trigger traced to launch control (FUN_7C8F4 / FUN_28618). Was "ETV 2 - 7".

REFERENCE: data @0x1A92D4, X axis @0x19079C, Y axis @0x1A9284, descriptor @0x18FBA0, code FUN_7c8c2.</description>
