    <description>DECODED (v5, confidence LOW): FUN_509A2: copied to fef015B4 for mode A (option 0x18B778).

Previous title: Variant RPM threshold A @0x18B66C

Scalar (not in descriptor table). RPM = X/2.56. 10L1=9728 (3800 rpm), 10L4=9472 (3700 rpm). Meaning unconfirmed - compare both bins before changing.

Read by FUN_509A2, a mode/gear-dependent feature: mode byte 0x18B778 (10L1 = 2 = enabled conditionally, 10L4 = 0 = OFF) and the bytes after it select when the feature is active, comparing the gear bitmask (RAM 0xFEF026C2) with 0x18B77A-0x18B77C. When active it sets flag RAM 0xFEF015C8 bit0 and swaps in the RPM pair 0x18B670/72 or 0x18B674/76 (default pair 0x18B66C/6E) as working thresholds (RAM 0xFEF015B4/B6). In the 10L4 (your bike) the feature is switched off, so only the default pair is used.</description>
