  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x20001" flags="0x0">
    <title>Decel Fuel Cut :: Resume RPM (Gear x Cylinder)</title>
    <description>Decel fuel-cut RPM band per gear and cylinder (warm engine). FUN_49E10 picks one row each cycle: clutch pulled (FUN_7626A) -&gt; "Clutch-in"; neutral or FUN_365B8 -&gt; "Neutral / other"; otherwise the row for the engaged gear. Each cell is a pair: RESUME RPM (lower edge, fef01270) and CUT RPM (upper edge, fef01268). FUN_4A256 runs the cut state machine with that band (closed throttle / decel conditions decided elsewhere). Cold engine (ECT &lt;= 0x1826A3) uses the separate "Decel Fuel Cut :: Cold | ..." constants instead. Stock clutch-in row = 25200/25300 rpm = no decel cut with the clutch pulled. Raise both values to stop decel fuel-cut in that gear (e.g. for a smoother corner entry or to keep fuel in the exhaust); keep CUT &gt; RESUME.

This table: RESUME (lower) RPM. Data 0x18251C, 8 rows x 4 cyl, 32-bit stride (interleaved with the CUT table).</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="15" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="2" />
