  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x2009E" flags="0x0">
    <title>DTC Monitor Enable :: P0120 - TP sensor 1 circuit</title>
    <description>Ticked (0x80) = the ECU runs this diagnostic monitor and can set P0120. Unticked (0x00) = the monitor is skipped: the code never sets, no lamp, and the fault-driven fail-safe for it is not triggered. The same byte also tells the OBD service whether the monitor is supported (FUN_11010).
CAUTION: this monitor protects the throttle-by-wire / engine-position / ECM integrity / oil-pressure system. Turning it off hides a real fault and can stop the ECU from entering its fail-safe (for wheel-speed codes: traction/launch control keep running on bad data). Not recommended.

DTCs controlled by this byte: P0120 - TP sensor 1 circuit.
STOCK (5JCZSJ30): 0x80 (monitor ON). Several stock calibrations ship with many emissions monitors switched off.
ADDRESS 0x154961. Monitor code checks "byte == 0x80" (example: FUN_32A24 for P2123). Use a full byte value of 0x80 or 0x00 - other values also count as OFF.
Related: the lamp toggles in "Diagnostics - DTC Lamp Control" only hide the lamp; this switch stops the monitor itself.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x154961" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x80</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
