  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x200BF" flags="0x0">
    <title>DTC Monitor Enable :: P2120 - APS sensor 1 circuit</title>
    <description>Ticked (0x80) = the ECU runs this diagnostic monitor and can set P2120. Unticked (0x00) = the monitor is skipped: the code never sets, no lamp, and the fault-driven fail-safe for it is not triggered. The same byte also tells the OBD service whether the monitor is supported (FUN_11010).
CAUTION: this monitor protects the throttle-by-wire / engine-position / ECM integrity / oil-pressure system. Turning it off hides a real fault and can stop the ECU from entering its fail-safe (for wheel-speed codes: traction/launch control keep running on bad data). Not recommended.

DTCs controlled by this byte: P2120 - APS sensor 1 circuit.
