    <title>DTC Monitor Enable :: P0500 #3 - Vehicle speed sensor (front wheel speed from ABS unit)</title>
    <description>Ticked (0x80) = the ECU runs this diagnostic monitor and can set P0500 #3. Unticked (0x00) = the monitor is skipped: the code never sets, no lamp, and the fault-driven fail-safe for it is not triggered. The same byte also tells the OBD service whether the monitor is supported (FUN_11010).
CAUTION: this monitor protects the throttle-by-wire / engine-position / ECM integrity / oil-pressure system. Turning it off hides a real fault and can stop the ECU from entering its fail-safe (for wheel-speed codes: traction/launch control keep running on bad data). Not recommended.

