  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x200F0" flags="0x0">
    <title>DTC Monitor Enable :: (info) DTCs with no enable byte</title>
    <description>These DTCs are hard-coded as supported/enabled (constant 0x80 in FUN_11010) and have no calibration switch - use the lamp toggle or the monitor thresholds instead: P0607 - ECM performance (internal processor); P0106 #1 - IAP/MAP sensor range/performance (not in Gen3 manual); P0138 - HO2 sensor B1S2 high (not used); P0136 - HO2 sensor B1S2 circuit (not used); P2A01 - HO2 sensor B1S2 range (not used); P0139 - HO2 sensor B1S2 slow (not used); P0158 - HO2 sensor B2S2 high (not used); P0156 - HO2 sensor B2S2 circuit (not used); P2A04 - HO2 sensor B2S2 range (not used); P0159 - HO2 sensor B2S2 slow (not used); P2102 - Throttle actuator (ETV motor) circuit low; P2101 - Throttle actuator (ETV motor) range/performance; P0036 - HO2 heater B1S2 (not used); P0056 - HO2 heater B2S2 (not used); P0010 - Cam actuator circuit (not used - no VVT); P003C - Cam profile actuator (not used); P0505 - Idle air control system (not in Gen3 manual); P0420 - Catalyst efficiency bank 1 (not in Gen3 manual); P0430 - Catalyst efficiency bank 2 (not in Gen3 manual); P0602 - ECM programming error - none (group 0x10) enabled.

This constant just re-displays the P1622 enable byte (0x1549F5) so the note has somewhere to live.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" />
